{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All assets cloned. Now **Step 2: build core UI components**: Button (with Hover variant), TextField (Default/Focused/Textarea), Logo, NavItem, IconButton, SectionLink (\"Learn more\" link).\n\nI'll write a call that:\n1. Loads fonts.\n2. Finds cloned components by id (I have ids: Button 7:2, TextField 7:4, Logo_Mark 7:8, Icon_Arrow_Right 7:13, Icon_Chevron_Down 7:28, Icon_Chevron_Left 7:30, Icon_Chevron_Right 7:32).\n3. Reposition originals; build:\n\n**Button variants**: clone Button comp (7:2) → keep as \"Button\" default. Create Hover variant: clone, darken fill #F09D05, put both in ComponentSet \"Button\" with prop State=Default/Hover.\n- componentSet = figma.combineAsVariants([default, hover], page); set name \"Button\", position.\n- Variant naming: set node.name = 'State=Default' and 'State=Hover' before combining.\n\n**TextField variants**: 7:4 (Label + Input + Placeholder). \n- Default: rename State=Default, set Label text.\n- Focused: clone, Input stroke brand 2px, maybe subtle shadow. State=Focused.\n- Textarea: clone, height 152 (label + input 120), placeholder \"Hello, I am interested in…\" — name State=Textarea? Variant prop same: State=Default/Focused/Textarea is mixing state+type; acceptable pragmatically but cleaner: two props. combineAsVariants requires names \"Prop=Value\". I'll use two props: State=Default|Focused|Filled? Keep simple: State=Default, State=Focused, Type=Textarea — combineAsVariants parses names with comma: \"State=Default, Type=Field\". I'll do: default \"State=Default, Type=Field\", focused \"State=Focused, Type=Field\", textarea \"State=Default, Type=Textarea\". Combine into set \"Text Field\".\n- Textarea input height 120, placeholder \"Hello, I am interested in…\".\n\nInstance creation helper later: `defaultComp.createInstance()` then override text.\n\n**Logo component**: frame 200x40? auto-layout horizontal gap 12, center: Logo_Mark instance (11x33 — small; scale up 1.5x? Instance resize: 16.5x49.5? The mark is very slim; scale to h=40: w=13.3. Let me set 14x42? Keep aspect 11:33 = 1:3. Height 36 → w 12. Wordmark \"NORTHGATE\" DM Sans Bold 22, letterSpacing 8%, ink. Logo comp: auto-layout H, itemSpacing 12, padding 0, alignment center, height 48, width hug. For footer reuse (colors: mark amber same, text ink on light footer fine).\n\n**NavItem**: auto-layout frame padding 8x12? Text \"Buy\" DM Sans Medium 16. Variants Current=No/Yes: No → muted ink color? Nav default ink; current = brand amber + maybe underline bar. Build two comps: \"Current=No\" (ink), \"Current=Yes\" (brand + 2px underline offset? add small rounded rect under). Combine as set \"Nav Item\".\n\n**IconButton**: 48x48 circle, stroke border, center icon instance (chevron left default). Variants State=Default/Hover? Keep single; two uses (prev/next) — chevron swap per instance. Name \"Icon Button\".\n\n**SectionLink** (\"Learn more\"): auto-layout H gap 8 center: text \"Learn more\" SemiBold 16 brand + Icon_Arrow_Right instance 24x12 (recolor vector to brand? The icon stroke is ink; override nested vector stroke to brand). Name \"Text Link\".\n\nWait — icon recoloring inside instances: nested vector strokes override allowed. I'll do `inst.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR')` set strokes.\n\nAlso recolor Icon_Arrow_Right used in footer/CTA (ink on amber) — override per instance as needed.\n\nPositions: Components zone at top (y 0..~1400 where cloned assets are). I'll place new component sets starting at x=0, y=900? The cloned assets grid occupied ~4 rows * ~500 = maybe 2100px tall. Let me place new components at y=2600, x spread. Frames 01_Home at y=3400, 02_Property at x=1600,y=3400. Fine.\n\nAlso design token text? Skip.\n\nLet me now also fix: original cloned Button (7:2) has child text \"Button\" 54 wide with auto-layout — text alignment centered? w=180 h=56, al HORIZONTAL. Text \"Button\". I'll set paddings: primaryButton padding 24/16, center. Resize to hug width: set layout: primaryAutoLayoutAxisAlignment center, primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO, counterAxisSizingMode AUTO, itemSpacing 8. Set text characters \"Button\".\n\nFor instances: override text characters (need font loaded — loaded).\n\nNow write Call 2 code carefully. Key API points:\n- figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent) → ComponentSetNode.\n- Setting name with \"=\" before combining → becomes variant props.\n- ComponentSet name \"Button\".\n\nCode sketch:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:s})));\nconst get = id => figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\nconst C = {}; // comps\nC.btn = await get('7:2'); C.tf = await get('7:4'); C.logoMark = await get('7:8');\nC.arrow = await get('7:13'); C.chevD = await get('7:28'); C.chevL = await get('7:30'); C.chevR = await get('7:32');\n\n// palette\nconst BRAND={r:1,g:0.6745,b:0.0706}, BRAND_H={r:0.937,g:0.592,b:0.020}; // #EF9705? compute: E9=233/255=0.9137, 99=153/255=0.6, 06=6/255=0.0235. use those\nconst INK={r:0.102,g:0.102,b:0.122};\n\n// BUTTON\nconst btnD = C.btn; btnD.name='State=Default';\nbtnD.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; btnD.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; btnD.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\nbtnD.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; btnD.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\nbtnD.paddingLeft=btnD.paddingRight=28; btnD.paddingTop=btnD.paddingBottom=16; btnD.itemSpacing=10;\n// resize height ~56: text 21 + 32 = 53; set paddings 17.5 -> 56. use 17/17? make paddingTop/Bottom 17 => 55. hmm set 17.5 allowed? paddings accept floats. 17.5*2+21=56.\nbtnD.paddingTop=17.5; btnD.paddingBottom=17.5;\nconst btnHover = btnD.clone(); btnHover.name='State=Hover';\nbtnHover.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:BRAND_H}];\nconst btnSet = figma.combineAsVariants([btnD,btnHover], page);\nbtnSet.name='Button'; \n```\n\nWait: combineAsVariants moves nodes into set; the set is added to page. Position set.x=0,y=2600.\n\nAdd arrow icon into button? I'll add hidden icon instance inside both variants:\n```js\nfunction addArrow(btn, comp, visible){ const a = comp.createInstance(); btn.appendChild(a); a.name='Icon_Arrow_Right'; a.visible=visible; recolorStroke(a, BRAND or INK); }\n```\nBut button uses auto-layout centered; adding icon increases width — with visible=false, auto-layout skips hidden children. \n\nDefault button arrow color: ink (on amber). Contact agent button: arrow ink. Hero \"See all listings\": arrow ink. OK arrow ink always in button.\n\nInstance overrides later: find child text instance? Text child name 'Button'; in instance: `inst.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT')`.characters = ...; set visible of icon: `inst.findOne(n=>n.name==='Icon_Arrow_Right').visible=true`.\n\nTEXT FIELD:\n```js\nconst tfD = C.tf; tfD.name='State=Default, Type=Field';\ntfD.itemSpacing=8; // label to input gap (label at y0, input y26 → gap 26-18=8)\ntfD.paddingLeft=0... paddings 0.\n```\nLabel text: 'Label' Bold 14 ink. Keep.\nFocused: clone → Input strokes brand 2, add subtle effect drop shadow rgba brand 25% 0 0 3? Simple: stroke brand 1.5? Use strokeWeight 2 + stroke brand.\nTextarea: clone of D → input height 120, input layoutMode VERTICAL? placeholder top-left: input counterAxisAlignItems 'MIN', primaryAxisAlignItems 'MIN'; placeholder text \"Hello, I am interested in…\".\nNames: 'State=Default, Type=Textarea'.\nCombine 3 → set 'Text Field'.\n\nLOGO:\n```js\nconst lg = figma.createComponent(); lg.name='Logo';\nlg.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; lg.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; lg.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; lg.itemSpacing=12;\nlg.fills=[];\nconst mi = C.logoMark.createInstance(); lg.appendChild(mi); mi.resize(12,36);\nconst wm = figma.createText(); wm.fontName={family:'DM Sans',style:'Bold'}; wm.characters='NORTHGATE'; wm.fontSize=24; wm.letterSpacing={unit:'PERCENT',value:10}; wm.fills=[solid(INK)];\nlg.appendChild(wm);\nlg.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; lg.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\n```\n\nNAV ITEM:\n```js\nfunction navItem(label, current){ const c=figma.createComponent(); c.name= current?'Current=Yes':'Current=No'; c.layoutMode='VERTICAL'; c.itemSpacing=6; c.fills=[]; c.paddingLeft=c.paddingRight=2;\n const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'DM Sans',style:'Medium'}; t.fontSize=16; t.characters=label; t.fills=[solid(current?BRAND:INK)]; c.appendChild(t);\n if(current){ const bar=figma.createRectangle(); bar.resize(t.width,3); bar.cornerRadius=2; bar.fills=[solid(BRAND)]; c.appendChild(bar);} else { const bar=figma.createRectangle(); bar.resize(t.width,0)... } \n```\nHmm variants of a set must have same structure ideally. Non-current: invisible spacer bar? Height 0 rect fine. Or skip bar; combineAsVariants doesn't require same. I'll add bar 3px brand for Yes; for No add transparent bar 3px (fills []). Nav label fixed 'Buy'; instances override text.\n\nICON BUTTON:\n```js\nconst ib = figma.createComponent(); ib.name='Icon Button'; ib.resize(48,48); ib.cornerRadius=24; ib.fills=[solid(white)]; ib.strokes=[solid(BORDER)];\nconst ci = C.chevL.createInstance(); ib.appendChild(ci); ci.x=(48-24)/2; ci.y=12;\n```\nchevron left comp is 24x24? metadata: Icon_Chevron_Left symbol w24 h24? The frame listing said symbol 3:10 w:24 h:24? It said Icon_Chevron_Left x54.5 y14 w24 h24 in frame 133x75 — yes 24x24. Center y=(48-24)/2=12.\n\nTEXT LINK:\n```js\nconst tl = figma.createComponent(); tl.name='Text Link'; tl.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; tl.itemSpacing=10; tl.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; tl.fills=[];\nconst t='Learn more' SemiBold 16 BRAND; const a=C.arrow.createInstance() recolored stroke BRAND; tl.appendChild(t); tl.appendChild(a);\ntl.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; tl.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\n```\nrecolorStroke helper: `a.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR').forEach(v=>v.strokes=[solid(BRAND)])`. ArrowRight stroke is the line; fills empty. Good.\n\nPosition sets: place all new comps/sets in a row at y=2600: btnSet.x=0; tfSet.x=260; logo.x=800; navSet.x=1100; ib.x=1350; tl.x=1450. Heights vary. Fine-tune: btnSet ~56 tall at y2600; tfSet 74; logo 40 → align tops y2600.\n\nReturn ids JSON for later: {btnDefault, btnHover, btnSet, tfDefault, tfFocused, tfTextarea, tfSet, logo, navNo, navYes, navSet, iconBtn, textLink}.\n\nI'll record returned ids. Later calls reference components by id via getNodeByIdAsync.\n\nOne concern: combineAsVariants requires variants have unique prop combos & names formatted 'Prop=Value'. Comma-space separator. OK.\n\nAlso: after combineAsVariants, the set's children components get variantProps. The original component 7:2 remains separate (it's the base we cloned from? Actually btnD IS 7:2 renamed). Hmm — 7:2 was my cloned Button from reference; I rename it to 'State=Default' and combine → set contains it. Good, no stray.\n\nSimilarly tf 7:4 becomes 'State=Default, Type=Field' inside set.\n\nFont loads: Bold for label/wordmark, Medium, SemiBold, Regular.\n\nletterSpacing PERCENT. lineHeight: set for texts: I'll skip line height except paragraphs later.\n\nWrite the call now. Also include solid() helper: `const solid=c=>({type:'SOLID',color:c});`","signature":"e4a26d7b87044c63906638f4"}],"id":"c9523785-37c8-4216-b88e-133ac61ce5f3","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78243550-d1f1-4909-8c2b-393b72e47362","uuid":"34ba1dcb-d704-400a-91a5-dc05648d4025","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:46:55.575Z","thinking_duration_ms":74243}
