ld'.\n\nValue text default 'Any'? For frame: Looking for → 'Buy or rent'? Hmm copy invention... The filters' values aren't specified; label is specified. Default value placeholder: use label-ish generic. I'll set value text per instance: Looking for: 'Buy'; Location: 'Brooklyn, NY'; Property type: 'House'; Price: 'Any price'. Wait — data copy accuracy: inventing filter values is \"design decision\"? The must-include says filters \"Looking for · Location · Property Type · Price (Icon_Chevron_Down)\". Values unspecified → mine to choose. Reasonable demo values ok. I'll use: Looking for → 'Buy'; Location → 'New York, NY'; Property Type → 'House'; Price → 'Any price'. Hmm, address is Brooklyn; use 'Brooklyn, NY'. OK.\n\nMenu options for Open variant: generic ['Any','House','Apartment'] — but state not used in frame; fine.\n\nStatTile: HORIZONTAL? VERTICAL gap 10: icon instance 24x24 area (icons 16x16 except bed 14x11, arrow 24x12, chevrons 24x24) — resize icon to 24? Scaling vector icons: resize instance scales strokes? Icon 16x16 → 24x24 strokeWeight stays 1.33? Instance resize scales children proportionally? Resizing an instance doesn't scale children unless constraints SCALE. Icons may not have SCALE constraints. Safer: keep icon native size (16x16, bed 14x11), inside 40x40 tile bg? StatTile: icon 16 native in a 44x44 rounded square bgWarm center, then number+label right? Layout: HORIZONTAL gap 14 center: iconBox 44x44 radius 8 bg #FAF8F4 center icon; VERTICAL gap 2: number 22 Bold ink, label 14 Regular ink2.\n- Default icon: Icon_Bed instance; per instance swap to Bath/Garage/Floors/Calendar. Number/label override.\n\nFeatureItem: HORIZONTAL gap 10 center: Icon_Check instance (16x16 native) + text 15 Regular ink. Component 'Feature Item'.\n\nTestimonialClient: HORIZONTAL gap 14 center: Avatar_Client instance 56x56 (resize; image fill FILL ok) cornerRadius 28; VERTICAL gap 2: name 16 SemiBold, 'Client' 14. Variants: Current=No (name ink2? name ink, role muted) / Current=Yes (name ink Bold? + role BRAND + small dot?). Design: Current: role text amber + name ink SemiBold; Default: role muted, name ink2? Hmm hierarchy: current emphasized: name ink SemiBold, role BRAND SemiBold; default: name ink2 Medium, role muted. Add amber dot before name for current? Keep simple: role color differs. Also avatar default slightly desaturated? no.\n\nGalleryThumb: component 'Gallery Thumb': frame 176x120 radius 10, clipsContent true, photo instance fill (Photo_Modern_House_1 default), stroke border 1. Variants State=Default / State=Selected: Selected stroke BRAND 2. Per instance swap photo.\n\nSearchBar: not component? Build directly in frame. It's listed as business component to build reusable: 'Search Filter Bar' component: HORIZONTAL padding 12 gap 8, bg white, radius 12, border: 4 FilterField instances (widths flexible via layoutGrow) + separators. Width 1312. Each FilterField instance layoutGrow=1. Between fields divider 1x40 rect fill BORDER. But FilterField component itself contains label+row; instance resizing: set width via layoutGrow. OK — component instances can layoutGrow.\n\nHmm, FilterField as component with fixed width 280 then in bar instance layoutGrow 1 → stretches. Value row space-between inside. Good.\n\nLet me also create 'Section Heading'? skip.\n\nIDs needed: photos listing 7:54..7:58,7:66; icons bed 7:19, bath 7:15, area 7:10, check 7:25, chevD 7:28; avatar client 7:48; modern house photos 7:59-7:67.\n\nCall 4 code — sizable. Let me write carefully.\n\nPositions: y=3800 row for these; x spread.\n\nListingCard:\n```\nconst card=figma.createComponent(); card.name='Listing Card'; card.resize(416,340);\ncard.layoutMode='VERTICAL'; card.itemSpacing=0; card.fills=[solid(WHITE)]; card.cornerRadius=12;\ncard.strokes=[solid(BORDER)]; card.strokeWeight=1; card.clipsContent=true;\ncard.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; card.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';\nconst ph=photoL1.createInstance(); card.appendChild(ph); ph.name='Photo'; ph.layoutAlign='STRETCH'; ph.resize(416,240); // after stretch, height fixed 240\n```\nInstance resize with layoutAlign STRETCH: width follows container; height stays as set. In component itself container width 416 → photo 416x240.\n\nbody:\n```\nconst body=figma.createFrame(); body.name='Body'; body.fills=[]; body.layoutMode='VERTICAL'; body.itemSpacing=12; body.paddingTop=18; body.paddingBottom=20; body.paddingLeft=22; body.paddingRight=22; body.layoutAlign='STRETCH'; body.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; body.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\nname text 20 SemiBold 'Property name' name='Name';\nmeta H gap 18 center: three groups (H gap 6 center): icon+text.\n```\nmeta texts: '4 bd','2 ba','1,650 sq ft' named 'Bed','Bath','Area'. icons: bed (14x11), bath (16x16), area (16x16) native size. Keep ink color native.\n\nicon vertical alignment: center row.\n\nCard default name 'Malto House'? Make generic 'Property'; override per instance. Default = first listing to save overrides: name 'Malto House', meta '4 bd','2 ba','1,650 sq ft', photo Listing_1. Instances 2..6 swap photo+texts.\n\nFilterField:\n```\nfunction filterField(open){\n const c=figma.createComponent(); c.name= open?'State=Open':'State=Default';\n c.layoutMode='VERTICAL'; c.itemSpacing=6; c.fills=[]; c.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; c.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED'; c.resize(280, open? 200: 64);\n const lb= await text('Label',13,'SemiBold',MUTED,'Label');\n c.appendChild(lb);\n const row=figma.createFrame(); row.name='Value Row'; row.fills=[]; row.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; row.primaryAxisAlignItems='SPACE_BETWEEN'; row.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; row.layoutAlign='STRETCH'; row.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED'; row.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\n const val= await text('Any price',16,'Medium',INK,'Value'); row.appendChild(val);\n const chev=chevD.createInstance(); row.appendChild(chev); chev.name='Chevron';\n c.appendChild(row);\n if(open){ menu... }\n return c;\n}\n```\nMenu: VERTICAL gap 0, radius 10, border, white fill, shadow effect, padding 6, width 280: 3 rows: text 15 padding 10x12 each option row frame hover none. Options 'Any price','$300k–$500k','$500k+'? generic — fine (not shown in frame).\n\nShadow: {type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r:0.06,g:0.06,b:0.08,a:0.10}, offset:{x:0,y:12}, radius:24, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}.\n\ncombineAsVariants([d,o]) name 'Filter Field'.\n\nStatTile:\n```\nconst st=figma.createComponent(); st.name='Stat Tile'; st.fills=[];\nst.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; st.itemSpacing=14; st.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; st.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; st.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\nconst box=figma.createFrame(); box.name='Icon Box'; box.resize(44,44); box.cornerRadius=10; box.fills=[solid(WARM)]; box.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL'; box.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER'; box.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\nconst ic=bedComp.createInstance(); box.appendChild(ic); ic.name='Icon'; st.appendChild(box);\nconst col=figma.createFrame(); col.fills=[]; col.layoutMode='VERTICAL'; col.itemSpacing=2; col.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; col.counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO';\ncol.appendChild(await text('4',22,'Bold',INK,'Number'));\ncol.appendChild(await text('Bedrooms',14,'Regular',INK2,'Label'));\nst.appendChild(col);\n```\n\nFeatureItem: H gap 10 center: check instance + text 15 'Air conditioning' name 'Label'.\n\nTestimonialClient variants:\n```\nfunction tclient(current){\n c=figma.createComponent(); c.name= current?'Current=Yes':'Current=No'; H gap 14 center; fills [];\n av=avatarClient.createInstance(); av.resize(56,56); av.cornerRadius=28; av.name='Avatar'; c.appendChild(av);\n col: name 16 SemiBold current?INK:INK2 name 'Name' chars 'Leo Madrigal'; role 14 current?'SemiBold':'Regular' color current?BRAND:MUTED chars 'Client' name 'Role';\n}\ncombine → 'Testimonial Client'.\n```\n\nGalleryThumb variants:\n```\nfunction thumb(selected){ c=figma.createComponent(); c.name=selected?'State=Selected':'State=Default'; c.resize(176,120); c.cornerRadius=10; c.clipsContent=true; c.fills=[solid(WHITE)];\n c.strokes=[solid(selected?BRAND:BORDER)]; c.strokeWeight= selected?2:1;\n photo MH1 instance name 'Photo'; stretch: x0 y0 resize 176x120;\n}\n```\nUse constraints? In component: photo child constraints SCALE? set child.constraints={horizontal:'SCALE',vertical:'SCALE'} so instance resize keeps fill. resize photo to 176x120 with image fill FILL.\n\nAll good. Also I need WARM color: #FAF8F4 = r0.980,g0.969,b0.949. MUTED #8B8B94 r0.545,g0.545,b0.580.\n\nLet me write Call 4. Long but manageable. Also position comps at y=3800 row.","signature":"32b5a1b79cc14865b5cf83df"}],"id":"651c6e64-36e2-47fd-a1bc-d2389a213a6b","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78243550-d1f1-4909-8c2b-393b72e47362","uuid":"1a181734-b7a5-4f29-8255-f902def07c84","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:49:14.555Z","thinking_duration_ms":57424}
