ation is 'NAVIGATE'? Hmm.\n\nWait — branch order: the union member that has transition is likely type 'NAVIGATE' with destinationId... but destinationId was listed as unrecognized in ALL branches? The error says \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" for branch BACK/CLOSE. For other branches similar. But the transition branch would have shown its own type expectation. The message for that branch: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following\" — it doesn't say type was invalid, meaning maybe in that branch type matched! Which type has a transition but no destinationId complaint? Possibly the action type is... Hmm.\n\nLet me think about what schema this MCP validator uses. Maybe it's based on the Figma REST-like \"PrototypePostMessage\" or the new \"figma.widget\" schema. Common action shapes:\n- {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition}  ← standard plugin API\n- {type:'NAVIGATE', destinationId, transition}? \n\nHmm, maybe this validator expects action.type 'NAVIGATE'? But branch 2 said \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" — that's just one branch for a simple action. The transition branch might expect type 'NAVIGATE'... but then destinationId would be flagged as unrecognized unless that branch expects destinationId.\n\nActually, notice: for the transition branch, the only complaint is about transition — meaning within that branch, type:'NODE'?? No wait. If type NODE matched that branch, destinationId and navigation would need to be recognized too... but no complaint about them in that branch. Hmm — the zod error aggregation shows per-branch issues. The transition branch's issues only mention transition. So in that branch: type 'NODE' OK? destinationId OK? navigation OK? but transition invalid because 'INSTANT' isn't in enum.\n\nThat makes sense! The NODE action exists with destinationId + navigation + transition, but transition must be one of DISSOLVE/SMART_ANIM