xtAutoResize='HEIGHT' → resize(w,10). When textAutoResize is 'WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT', resize sets both. Then switching to 'HEIGHT' should recompute height on next reflow... apparently it kept 10? or resize set height 10 AFTER switching mode, and with HEIGHT mode resize(w,h)... per docs resize() on text with HEIGHT: \"the height argument is ignored\". Evidently NOT ignored — height stayed 10.\n\nRobust fix: use `t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'` then set width via `t.resize(w, t.height)`? Same issue. Better: after setting text+width, force recompute: set `t.textAutoResize='NONE'` then resize(w,10) then 'HEIGHT'? Hmm.\n\nCleanest known-good approach: create text, set font/size/characters/lineHeight, set textAutoResize='HEIGHT', then resize(w, 100) — if ignored, height auto-computes. The evidence says height stayed 10. Alternative: the sandbox recomputes lazily and only on render — but screenshots show 10px heights.\n\nAlternative reliable method: `t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(w, t.height)` — if the API ignores height param, works; if not, keeps current height (which after characters set = one line height ~ for auto W_H). Actually when textAutoResize='WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT', after characters the node height = text height (single line, since width unconstrained). Then switching to HEIGHT + resize(w, currentHeight)... height param ignored? Should reflow to multi-line height. The current evidence contradicts.\n\nHmm wait, let me re-examine: maybe height DID reflow but the OVERLAP comes from something else. Property description: para1 \"A bright, single-storey family home on a quiet tree-lined street, a short walk from Foster Avenue's cafés and\" — then overlap \"the subway\" over para2. Para1 at width 800: full text is ~2 lines. dsec V layout itemSpacing 16. If para1.height=2 lines (~52), para2 at +16 below. Overlap means para1.height ~26 (1 line) while text wraps to 2 lines. So height stayed ONE line — consistent with height not recomputed after width change from unconstrained to 800.\n\nTheory: `resize(w,h)` on text with autoResize='HEIGHT' behaves like WIDTH fixed, height = h param (docs say for HEIGHT mode you should use resize without respecting h? or use `resize` where h ignored...). Evidently h=10 or 40 STUCK (agency copy shows ~2.5 lines visible before overlap — actually agency copy shows 2 lines + clipped 3rd? It shows \"...buy, sell and\" / \"team\" clipped... hmm it shows text cut mid-line then \"Learn more\" overlapping. That suggests height ~40 (I resized hcp to (560,40))! YES — agency copy: resize(560,40) → height 40 = 2 lines visible, rest clipped. Hero copy: resize(560,40) — hero shows 2 lines fully (fits in 40). Quote: resize(880,10) → 10px?? but 3 lines show... contradiction!\n\nUgh. Wait — quote: I resized to (880,10) AFTER setting autoResize? If h ignored → auto. If h stuck → 10px showing ~0 lines. Screenshot shows 3 lines. So for quote, h WAS ignored/auto. For agency copy (560,40): 40 stuck? It shows 2 lines then cut with overlap — 40px = 2 lines at lineHeight 28 = 56... 40px ≈ 1.4 lines. The render shows ~2 lines visible + \"Learn more\" overlapping line 2/3. Hmm.\n\nActually WAIT — maybe the overlap in agency/CTA/description is NOT text height but the CONTAINER heights: e.g., agency col now AUTO (hug) — col height = title(40)+20+copy.height+20+link. If copy.height=40 (stuck), then col = 40+40+20+20+~24=~144 — but the rendered agency text shows title, copy 2 lines clipped, Learn more ON the copy — meaning link position = 96+... hmm link overlapping copy means col layout: title y0, copy y60 (40 tall), link y120... that wouldn't overlap.\n\nUnless copy.height = 40 but text RENDER overflows its box? Text nodes with fixed height and autoResize NONE clip... no wait, if autoResize='HEIGHT' but height manually 40 → conflicts; render might draw all glyphs overflowing while layout uses 40. THAT matches: glyphs render fully (overflow visible), but layout box 40px → next sibling (link) placed at copy.y+40+20 → ON TOP of the overflo