{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN/ (fileKey rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN). Requirements:\n   - Assigned account confirmed via whoami: zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (already verified, user_id 1692091428764723877)\n   - Read 00 · Start Here (brief), 01 · Foundations (visual rules), reuse 02 · Components and 04 · Media assets; preserve all reference pages/nodes\n   - Deliver complete design inside 03 · Workspace (page 5:2); new frames/components/prototype links allowed there\n   - Build exactly 2 frames named \"01_Home\" and \"02_Property\" (1440 wide, light mode); all other components (header, footer, business components) as reusable components; required states (hover, focused field, selected thumbnail, current testimonial, open filter) exist as component variants\n   - Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim; brand #FFAC12 + DM Sans fixed\n   - Prototype links: 01_Home \"See all listings\" + each listing card → 02_Property; 02_Property header Logo → 01_Home; similar listing cards → 02_Property (platform blocks self-navigation — to be documented as limitation)\n   - Process: every assistant message with a tool call must start with \"Reasoning summary:\"; final response starts \"Reasoning summary:\" then \"Final answer:\" including assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations\n   - Use get_screenshot with enableBase64Response:true (no shell access) to verify; fix visible problems; unattended session — resolve routine choices from brief\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma; errors ROLL BACK the entire call (verified repeatedly) — always re-verify state after errors\n   - Sandbox quirks discovered: NO `size` property on nodes (use `.width`/`.height`); NO `componentId` on INSTANCE nodes; NO `createInstance()` on COMPONENT_SET (use `.defaultVariant.createInstance()`); text writes (including `textAutoResize` changes) require `figma.loadFontAsync` for the node's font first\n   - Reaction schema (validated): `node.reactions = [{ trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId:'<frameId>', navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null}] }]` — singular `action` field rejected (\"update the actions field\"); trigger 'CLICK' invalid (must be 'ON_CLICK'); transition 'INSTANT' invalid (use null)\n   - Same-frame prototype navigation is rejected: \"destinations must be a different top-level frame on the same page\" — similar cards inside 02_Property cannot navigate to 02_Property (both NAVIGATE and SWAP rejected)\n   - TEXT auto-height bug: `t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(w, small)` keeps the small height — glyphs overflow the box while layout uses the small height, causing sibling overlap. Candidate fix to test: toggle `textAutoResize='NONE'` then `'HEIGHT'` (with fonts loaded); fallback: manual heights (lines × lineHeight)\n   - Vertical auto-layout containers must use primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' (hug height); creating with resize(w, 0/10/100) + FIXED clips all children\n   - Sync text helper pattern (avoids the earlier un-awaited-promise appendChild bugs)\n   - `figma.combineAsVariants` sets; variant names contain a space after comma ('State=Default, Type=Field')\n   - Instance overrides: `inst.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.name==='X').characters=...`; nested photo swap via `photoInst.swapComponent(comp)`; button arrow via `inst.findOne(n=>n.name==='Icon_Arrow_Right').visible=true`\n   - layoutAlign='STRETCH' for full-width children; layoutGrow=1 for equal-width filter fields; layoutWrap='WRAP' + counterAxisSpacing for feature grid\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma file rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN pages: 0:1 (00 · Start Here), 1:2 (01 · Foundations), 1:3 (02 · Components), 1:4 (04 · Media), 5:2 (03 · Workspace — delivery target)\n   - THE TWO SCREEN FRAMES: **01_Home = 13:83** (at x=0,y=4600), **02_Property = 16:271** (at x=1600,y=4600)\n   - Component IDs on page 5:2: Button 7:2 (variant in set 8:7; hover variant 8:4), Text Field set 8:16 (variants 'State=Default, Type=Field' 7:4, 'State=Focused, Type=Field' 8:8, 'State=Default, Type=Textarea' 8:12; Label/Input/Placeholder child names), Logo 8:17, Nav Item set 8:25, Icon Button 8:26 (child 'Icon_Chevron'), Text Link 8:29, Header 9:5 (now FIXED 1440×88), Footer Column 9:22, Footer 9:28, Listing Card 12:39 (children 'Photo','Body'>'Name','Bed','Bath','Area'; meta icon instances named 'Icon'), Filter Field set 12:79 (default 12:60; children 'Label','Value Row'>'Value','Chevron'; 'Menu' in Open variant), Stat Tile 12:80 ('Icon Box'>'Icon','Number','Label'), Feature Item 12:88 ('Icon_Check','Label'), Testimonial Client set 12:103 (Current=No 12:93, Current=Yes 12:98; 'Name','Role'), Gallery Thumb set 12:108 (State=Default 12:104, State=Selected; 'Photo')\n   - Media asset components: 7:2 Button base, 7:4 TextField base, 7:8 Logo_Mark, 7:10 Icon_Area, 7:13 Icon_Arrow_Right, 7:15 Icon_Bath, 7:19 Icon_Bed, 7:22 Icon_Calendar, 7:25 Icon_Check, 7:28 Icon_Chevron_Down, 7:30 Icon_Chevron_Left, 7:32 Icon_Chevron_Right, 7:34 Icon_Floors, 7:37 Icon_Garage, 7:42/7:50/7:44 social logos (Facebook/Twitter/Instagram), 7:48 Avatar_Client, 7:49 Avatar_Kayley_Hall, 7:52 Photo_Agents_Meeting, 7:53 Photo_Hero_House, 7:54–7:58 Photo_Listing_1–5, 7:66 Photo_Listing_6, 7:59/7:67/7:60/7:61/7:62/7:63/7:64 Photo_Modern_House_1–7, 7:65 Photo_Modern_House_Main\n   - Key home IDs: hero button ('See all listings') 13:108; filter fields 14:82, 14:88, 14:94, 14:100; listing cards 14:108, 14:129, 14:150, 14:172, 14:193, 14:214; testimonial clients 15:219 (Leo Madrigal, Current=Yes), 15:224 (Owen Brooks), 15:229 (Mia Chen)\n   - Key property IDs: thumbs 16:299, 16:301, 16:303, 16:305, 16:307, 16:309, 16:311; header Logo instance I16:272;9:6; similar cards 17:620, 17:641, 17:662, 17:683\n   - Frame structure (names used for findOne): Home: 'Hero' (>'Hero Card'>'Photo_Hero_House','Overlay','Hero Content'), 'Agency Intro 1'/'Agency Intro 2' (>'Text','Photo_Agents_Meeting'), 'Listings' (>'Filter Bar' with 4 field instances layoutGrow=1, 'Grid'>'Row'×2 of cards), 'Testimonial' (>'Quote' text, 'Clients'), 'CTA' (>'Text' col, button), Footer instance. Property: header instance, 'Title Bar' (>'Left' with Title/Address, 'Right' with Price/PerSqft), 'Gallery' (>'Main Photo' 1312×540 r16, 'Thumbs'), 'Body' (>'Left' 824: 'Details' strip with 5 stat tiles, 'Description' 3 paras, 'Features' wrap grid of 15 items 264w; 'Right' 456: 'Agent Card' with Avatar 96 r48, Kayley Hall/Listing agent, 'View profile' link, Name/Phone/Email fields, Message textarea, 'Contact agent' button stretched), 'Similar' (>'Head' with title + 'Nav' with 2 icon buttons, 'Row' with 4 cards 310w), Footer instance\n   - Shared code pattern per call:\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:s})));\nconst get = id => figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\nconst solid = c => ({type:'SOLID',color:c});\nconst BRAND={r:1,g:0.6745,b:0.0706}, BRAND_H={r:0.9137,g:0.6,b:0.0235}, INK={r:0.102,g:0.102,b:0.122}, INK2={r:0.329,g:0.329,b:0.369}, MUTED={r:0.545,g:0.545,b:0.580}, BORDER={r:0.906,g:0.906,b:0.922}, WARM={r:0.980,g:0.969,b:0.949}, WHITE={r:1,g:1,b:1};\nfunction text(chars,size,style,color,name){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'DM Sans',style:style}; t.characters=chars; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[solid(color)]; if(name)t.name=name; return t; }  // SYNC — no await needed\n```\n   - Working prototype reaction:\n```js\nnode.reactions = [{ trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId:dest, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null}] }];\n```\n   - Verbatim copy applied: Hero 'Beautiful homes made for you' / 'Hand-picked homes, honest advice and a team that knows every street in the neighbourhoods we serve.'; Agency 1 'You’re in good hands' / 'Our agents have helped more than 2,000 families buy, sell and rent. We listen first, explain every step and stay with you until the keys are in your hand.'; Agency 2 'Local experts on every street' / 'We live where we work. From school catchments to the quietest blocks, we can tell you what the listing photos don’t.'; 'Find your next place to live'; filters Looking for/Buy, Location/Brooklyn, NY, Property Type/House, Price/Any price; Quote '“Kayley and the team found us a home we love in under a month. They knew every street, never pushed us, and we always felt in good hands.”'; CTA 'Ready to sell your home?' / 'Get a free valuation and a clear plan to sell at the right price, on your timeline.'; Property 'Modern House' / '3002 Foster Ave, Brooklyn, NY 11210, USA' / '$450,000' / '$280/sq ft'; stats 4 Bedrooms/2 Bathrooms/2 Garage/1 Floor/2007 Year built; description paras: 'A bright, single-storey family home on a quiet tree-lined street, a short walk from Foster Avenue’s cafés and the subway.' / 'The open-plan kitchen with a large island flows into the living and dining area, with floor-to-ceiling windows onto a private garden. Four bedrooms include a main suite with its own bathroom.' / 'Built in 2007 and updated in 2022, the house has a double garage, central air conditioning, new flooring throughout and plenty of built-in storage.'; 15 features (Air conditioning…Storage room); agent card Kayley Hall/Listing agent/View profile/Name-Your name/Phone-Your phone/Email-Your email/Message/'Contact agent'; 'Similar listings'\n   - Listing card data: home: Malto House 4bd/2ba/1,650 (7:54), Birchwood Villa 4/2/1,720 (7:55), Cedar Lane House 3/2/1,580 (7:56), Harbor View Loft 2/2/1,610 (7:57), Maple Court House 4/3/1,690 (7:58), Willow Creek Home 5/3/1,640 (7:66); similar: Malto House, Birchwood Villa, Cedar Lane House, Harbor View Loft (same first four)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - createInstance on COMPONENT_SET (12:79) → \"no such property 'createInstance' on COMPONENT_SET node\": fixed with `(await get('12:79')).defaultVariant.createInstance()`\n   - Wrong variant name 'State=Default,Type=Textarea' → findOne returned null → createInstance of null: actual names have a space after comma ('State=Default, Type=Textarea'); confirmed by listing set children\n   - Reaction schema errors (3 iterations): trigger 'CLICK' → must be 'ON_CLICK'; singular `action` → must be plural `actions` array; transition {type:'INSTANT'} → must be null; also `componentId` doesn't exist on INSTANCE in this sandbox (find children via named parents instead)\n   - Same-frame navigation rejected for similar cards (NAVIGATE and SWAP both) → left unwired, will document as platform limitation (cannot duplicate a third frame because brief requires exactly 2 frames)\n   - Systematic clipping bug: vertical auto-layout containers built with resize(w, 0/10/100) + primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED' clipped children (gallery invisible, description/features/agent card missing, listings overlapped, testimonial overlapped, CTA copy clipped); Header component hugged to ~747px. Fixed by setting primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' on ~11 containers and header to FIXED 1440×88\n   - TEXT auto-height bug (CURRENT): `textAutoResize='HEIGHT'` + resize(w, small) keeps small height; glyphs overflow and siblings overlap (agency copy ×2, quote, CTA copy, 3 description paras). Planned fix: toggle 'NONE'→'HEIGHT' with fonts loaded; fallback manual heights\n   - CTA button invisible: amber fill on amber CTA band — fix planned: instance root fills=[solid(WHITE)]\n   