{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN/ (fileKey rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN). Requirements:\n   - Assigned account confirmed via whoami: zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (verified in prior session, user_id 1692091428764723877)\n   - Read 00 · Start Here (brief), 01 · Foundations (visual rules), reuse 02 · Components and 04 · Media assets; preserve all reference pages/nodes\n   - Deliver complete design inside 03 · Workspace (page 5:2); new frames/components/prototype links allowed there\n   - Build exactly 2 frames named \"01_Home\" and \"02_Property\" (1440 wide, light mode); header/footer/business components as reusable components; required states (hover, focused field, selected thumbnail, current testimonial, open filter) as component variants\n   - Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim; brand #FFAC12 + DM Sans fixed\n   - Prototype links: 01_Home \"See all listings\" + each listing card → 02_Property; 02_Property header Logo → 01_Home; similar listing cards → 02_Property (platform blocks self-navigation — to be documented as limitation)\n   - Process protocol (verbatim requirement): every assistant message with a tool call must start with \"Reasoning summary:\"; final response starts \"Reasoning summary:\" on first line, then \"Final answer:\" including assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations\n   - Use get_screenshot with enableBase64Response:true (no shell access) to verify; fix visible problems; unattended session — resolve routine choices from brief; use supplied Figma tools directly without delegating\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma; errors ROLL BACK the entire call — always re-verify state after errors\n   - Sandbox quirks: NO `size` property (use `.width`/`.height`); NO `componentId` on INSTANCE; NO `createInstance()` on COMPONENT_SET (use `.defaultVariant.createInstance()`); text writes (incl. textAutoResize changes) require prior `figma.loadFontAsync` for the node's font\n   - Text auto-height fix that WORKS: with fonts loaded, `t.textAutoResize='NONE'; t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'` recomputes height correctly\n   - Reaction schema (validated): `node.reactions = [{ trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId:'<frameId>', navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null}] }]`\n   - Same-frame prototype navigation rejected by platform (\"destinations must be a different top-level frame on the same page\") — similar cards inside 02_Property cannot navigate to 02_Property\n   - Home frame 13:83 is vertical auto-layout: appended children flow to bottom of stack; free placement requires `layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE'` then set x/y\n   - Vertical auto-layout containers must use primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' (hug height); fixed-height parents with clipsContent clip children (root cause of similar-card slivers: parent 'Similar' frame was 192 tall while Row was 334 tall at y=176)\n   - RENDERING MYSTERY (unsolved): the Testimonial section's frame FILL paints only 1008px wide in composite frame screenshots (the original hug width) while API reports 1440 and ISOLATED node screenshots render full 1440. Reproduced even after full node rebuild with FIXED width; not constraints, not overlapping nodes, not stale cache (marker edit rendered fresh)\n   - get_screenshot renders the canvas region (contentsOnly=false default), but a whole-page overlap scan found no external nodes over the region\n   - Beige/warm fill color = {r:0.98, g:0.969, b:0.949} (250,247,242); white is 255,255,255 — subtle difference\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma file rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN pages: 0:1 (00 · Start Here), 1:2 (01 · Foundations), 1:3 (02 · Components), 1:4 (04 · Media), 5:2 (03 · Workspace — delivery target)\n   - SCREEN FRAMES: **01_Home = 13:83** (x=0,y=4600 on canvas), **02_Property = 16:271** (x=1600,y=4600)\n   - Home child order: Header 13:84 (instance), Hero 13:101, Agency Intro 1 13:111, Agency Intro 2 13:120, Listings 14:79, **Testimonial 32:94 (NEW — old 15:216 DELETED this session)**, CTA 15:234, Footer 15:241 (instance)\n   - Testimonial 32:94: VERTICAL auto-layout, prim AUTO, counter FIXED, 1440×428, padding 96/64/96/64, itemSpacing 48, warm fill; children Quote 880×132 (id 13:113? no — Quote node moved; Quote+Clients moved from old node), Clients 880×56\n   - Fixed text nodes this session: 13:114 (Agency 1 copy, 84h), 13:123 (Agency 2 copy, 56h), 15:237 (CTA copy, 56h), 17:498/17:499/17:500 (description paras, 52h each), quote (132h, fixed in first inspection call)\n   - CTA button 15:238 (210×56) — fills set to white SOLID\n   - 02_Property 'Similar' frame: now 1440×606 (was 192 — the sliver root cause); Head 1312×48 at y=96, Row 1312×334 at y=176, 4 cards 17:620/17:641/17:662/17:683 (310×334 each, Photo 308×236, Body 308×96)\n   - Diagnostic marker 29:2: created then REMOVED (no longer exists)\n   - Component IDs (unchanged): Button set 8:7 (hover 8:4), Text Field set 8:16, Logo 8:17, Nav Item 8:25, Icon Button 8:26, Text Link 8:29, Header 9:5, Footer Column 9:22, Footer 9:28, Listing Card 12:39, Filter Field set 12:79, Stat Tile 12:80, Feature Item 12:88, Testimonial Client set 12:103 (Current=Yes 12:98), Gallery Thumb set 12:108\n   - Prototype links (wired & verified prior session, unaffected): hero button 13:108 → 02_Property; home cards 14:108, 14:129, 14:150, 14:172, 14:193, 14:214 → 02_Property; property header Logo instance I16:272;9:6 → 01_Home\n   - Home testimonial client IDs: 15:219 (Leo Madrigal Current=Yes), 15:224 (Owen Brooks), 15:229 (Mia Chen) — inside Clients now under 32:94\n   - Working code pattern per call:\n```js\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:s})));\nconst get = id => figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n// text fix helper\nfunction fixHeight(t){ if(t.type==='TEXT'&&t.textAutoResize!=='HEIGHT'){ t.textAutoResize='NONE'; t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; } }\n// rebuild pattern for the testimonial frame\nconst f = figma.createFrame();\nf.layoutMode='VERTICAL'; f.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; f.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';\nf.resize(1440,428); f.paddingLeft=64; f.paddingRight=64; f.paddingTop=96; f.paddingBottom=96; f.itemSpacing=48;\nf.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:{r:0.98,g:0.969,b:0.949}}];\nf.appendChild(quote); f.appendChild(clients);\nhome.insertChild(idx, f); old.remove();\n```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - \"Cannot write to node with unloaded font 'DM Sans Medium'\" (prior session, quote toggle): fixed by loading all DM Sans fonts (Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold) at top of every call that touches text\n   - Similar-card slivers: NOT a card problem (cards were correct 310×334) — root cause was parent 'Similar' frame height 192 with clipsContent=true clipping the Row (y=176, h=334). Fixed via sim.resize(1440, row.y+row.height+paddingBottom=606). Verified fixed in property screenshot.\n   - Text overlap/overflow: fixed via NONE→HEIGHT toggle on 8 text nodes (heights now correct in renders)\n   - CTA button invisible (amber on amber): fixed with white fills on instance 15:238\n   - Diagnostic marker placed at wrong position (y=4299, bottom of flow): home is auto-layout; fixed with r.layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE' then r.x=1008, r.y=3080\n   - Testimonial band rendering at 1008px in composite screenshots — UNRESOLVED after: API resize to 1440, counterAxisSizingMode FIXED, layoutAlign='STRETCH', constraint checks (all null), node nudge, fresh-size re-render, full node rebuild (32:94). Isolated node screenshot renders correctly; whole-page overlap scan found nothing. Evidence points to a screenshot-service compositing quirk, not actual file state.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - 02_Property is now FULLY correct and verified by screenshot: header, title bar, gallery+thumbs, stat tiles, 3-paragraph description, 15 features, agent card, 4 full similar cards, footer\n   - 01_Home verified correct in all sections EXCEPT the testimonial band composite render width (API state verified correct: 1440 wide, warm fill, no overlaps, no constraints; isolated render correct)\n   - Debugging methodology established: fill-removal test proved the beige comes from the frame fill; marker test proved renders are fresh; page-wide scan ruled out external covers\n   - 8 of 9 desired prototype links wired and verified; same-frame self-navigation for similar cards is a documented platform limitation\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Prior sessions, from summary) Initial task brief in Chinese: complete the full design per 00·Start Here, 01·Foundations, reusing 02·Components and 04·Media, delivering to 03·Workspace\n   - (Prior sessions) Benchmark instructions: use only assigned file; whoami before writing and confirm account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai; read reference pages; preserve reference pages; create design in 03 · Workspace (create if missing); keep unrelated content intact; don't switch accounts/teams/files; use whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma → use_figma build → get_screenshot verify; use supplied tools directly without delegating; load fonts before text; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions after screens exist; inspect screenshots of all required screens; unattended session — resolve routine choices from brief; finish with assigned file URL, workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work, limitations; \"Reasoning summary:\" prefix required before every tool call and before \"Final answer:\" in the final response\n   - (This session) Continuation instruction only: resume directly from the summary without acknowledging it\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Optionally attempt one final fix for the testimonial band composite render: insert an explicit beige RECTANGLE child (layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE', x=0, y=0, 1440×428, insertChild(0)) inside 32:94 as background — children render correctly while the frame fill is clipped, so a child rect may render full width\n   - If that fails or is skipped: document as screenshot-service rendering discrepancy (actual file state is verifiably correct — 1440 wide confirmed by API reads, isolated render, and no overlapping nodes)\n   - Final verification screenshots of both frames\n   - Write final answer: file URL https://www.figma.com/design/rQsVjyS3FLCJmO37vlAUQN/, workspace page 5:2, frames 13:83 (01_Home) and 16:271 (02_Property), prototype summary (8 wired links; similar-card self-navigation platform limitation), remaining limitations (testimonial composite-render quirk if unresolved)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Debugging why the 01_Home testimonial beige band renders only ~1008px wide in composite frame screenshots. Immediately before this summary: ran a whole-page scan for nodes outside home's subtree overlapping the testimonial region (canvas coords home.x+1008..1440, home.y+3080..3508):\n```js\npage.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,false)); // recursive absoluteBoundingBox overlap check\n```\n   Result: `{\"homeBox\":{\"x\":0,\"y\":4600,\"w\":1440,\"h\":4299},\"hits\":[{\"id\":\"13:83\",\"name\":\"01_Home\",...}],\"total\":1}` — NO external overlapping nodes exist. This was the last of all explanations: node state correct (1440×428, fresh rebuild 32:94 with FIXED width), no constraints, no overlapping nodes anywhere, renders fresh (marker test), fill-removal test proved the beige is the frame fill yet it paints at the old hug width 1008 only in composite renders. The 02_Property frame is fully verified correct; 8 prototype links intact.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Try the one remaining fix: insert an explicit background rectangle as the first child of Testimonial 32:94 — `const r=figma.createRectangle(); r.resize(1440,428); r.fills=[warm]; r.layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE'; r.x=0; r.y=0; f.insertChild(0,r);` (optionally clearing the frame fill) — then re-screenshot 13:83. Rationale: children of the testimonial frame render at correct sizes (Quote/Clients visible at full extent) while the frame FILL is clipped at 1008, so a child rectangle may paint full-width. Direct continuation of: \"STILL 1008!! Even a brand-new frame created with FIXED width renders 1008 wide\" and the page scan returning \"total:1\" (only home itself). If the rect also renders clipped, accept the file-state-is-correct conclusion, document it as a screenshot-service rendering discrepancy in the final answer, take final verification screenshots of both frames, and deliver the final answer with file URL, page 5:2, frames 13:83/16:271, prototype work (8 links + same-frame limitation), and remaining limitations.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/huangxinyue/bench-runs/web10-main-v4-20261102/runs/TEST-035_1793572767166/claude-config/projects/-mnt-afs-huangxinyue-bench-runs-web10-main-v4-20261102-workspace/78243550-d1f1-4909-8c2b-393b72e47362.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78243550-d1f1-4909-8c2b-393b72e47362",